<title>RUSSIA: Russia Jan-Mar trade surplus widens to $7,00 bln.</title>
<headline>Russia Jan-Mar trade surplus widens to $7,00 bln.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia posted a trade surplus of $7.00 billion in the first quarter of this year after a $5.45 billion surplus in the same period of 1996, the State Statistics Committee said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Total trade, including other members of CIS</p>
<p>RUSSIAN MERCHANDISE TRADE Jan-Mar 97  Jan-Feb 97  Jan-Mar 96</p>
<p>    exports			    20.77	 13.59	 20.18</p>
<p>    imports			    13.77	  8.91	 14.72</p>
<p>    trade balance		    +7.00	 +4.69	 +5.45</p>
<p>Excluding trade with other members of CIS</p>
<p>RUSSIAN MERCHANDISE TRADE Jan-Mar 97  Jan-Feb 97  Jan-Mar 96</p>
<p>    exports			    16.50	 10.79	 15.66</p>
<p>    imports			    10.11	  6.38	 10.16</p>
<p>    trade balance		    +6.40	 +4.40	 +5.51</p>
<p>Notes -- Figures in billion dollars, FOB (differences due rounding).</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
